Great idea! Let's improve those page headings with better spacing and styling. Here's the CSS to add to your <style> section:

```css
/* Improved Page Headers - Better spacing and styling */
.section-header {
    margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
    padding-left: 0.5rem;
    border-left: 4px solid var(--accent);
    transition: var(--transition);
}

.section-header h2 {
    font-size: 1.75rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--primary);
    margin-bottom: 0.25rem;
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 0.5rem;
}

.section-header h2::before {
    content: '';
    display: inline-block;
    width: 8px;
    height: 28px;
    background: linear-gradient(135deg, var(--accent), var(--accent-light));
    border-radius: 4px;
}

.section-header p {
    color: #6c757d;
    margin-bottom: 0;
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    padding-left: 0.75rem;
}

/* Alternative if you want icons instead of the colored bar */
.section-header.with-icon h2::before {
    display: none;
}

.section-header.with-icon h2 i {
    font-size: 1.5rem;
    color: var(--accent);
}

/* Responsive adjustments */
@media (max-width: 768px) {
    .section-header {
        padding-left: 0.75rem;
        margin-bottom: 1.25rem;
    }
    
    .section-header h2 {
        font-size: 1.4rem;
    }
    
    .section-header h2::before {
        height: 24px;
    }
}
```

